# =====================================================================
# Release V084 -- Aggregate: drop NULL fk_Date rows at source (root fix for the 515)
# =====================================================================
# Root cause of the metric-actuals 515 (guarded downstream in V082/V083): the daily aggregate
# carried rows with NULL fk_Date. Confirmed on prod -- they are PENDING (unscheduled) appointments:
#   State='Pending', Start_Time=NULL  ->  Fact_Appointments.fk_Date_Start = NULL
#   (LEFT JOIN Dim_Date on CAST(Start_Time AS DATE), no match, no ISNULL(-1)).
# A pending appointment has no confirmed slot, so it belongs to NO day -- it must not be in the
# DAILY aggregate. It does have a resolved fk_Date_Pending (the booking day); a forward-book /
# pending metric should read that, not fk_Date_Start.
#
# Fix (one layer up from the metric-actuals symptom guards): filter NULL fk_Date at the two
# aggregate inserts, the single clean choke point --
#   * main insert (spine #apt_agg a)      -> WHERE a.fk_Date IS NOT NULL
#   * cancellation-only insert (#cancel_agg c) -> AND c.fk_Date IS NOT NULL (folded into its WHERE)
# Covers all source blocks (appointment/invoice/tp/diary) in one place, since every output row's
# fk_Date comes from the spine. Behaviour-neutral where data is clean (dev had 0 null-date rows).
#
# After this, the aggregate is clean and metric-actuals never sees a null; keep V082/V083 as
# belt-and-braces. Idempotent (DELETE + INSERT rebuild). No C#/catalog/schema change.
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V084__aggregate_drop_null_date_rows.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Site_Patient_Practitioner_Daily.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
